    "text": "All evidence is gathered. Here is the complete trace, with repository-relative paths and line numbers from this checkout.\n\n# Setup: what `zvec.init(optimize_threads=4)` configures\n\n- `python/zvec/zvec.py:29,38,162-163,173` \u2014 `init()` puts `optimize_threads` into `config_dict` and calls `Initialize(config_dict)`.\n- `src/binding/python/model/common/python_config.cc:153-158` \u2014 the binding requires `optimize_threads > 0` and sets `data.optimize_thread_count = 4`; `python_config.cc:192-193` applies it via `GlobalConfig::Instance().initialize(data)`.\n- `src/db/common/global_resource.cc:21-29` \u2014 a `std::call_once` lazily constructs the **global optimize pool** as `ailego::ThreadPool(GlobalConfig::Instance().optimize_thread_count(), \u2026)`; accessor at `src/db/common/global_resource.h:31-34`. The `ThreadPool` constructor clamps the request to `[1, hardware_concurrency]` (`src/ailego/parallel/thread_pool.cc:85-87, 93-101`); with hardware concurrency \u2265 4, the global pool holds **4 workers**.\n\nThe optimize call itself routes: `OptimizeOption` \u2192 `OptimizeOptions::concurrency_` (`src/binding/python/model/param/python_param.cc:2179-2202`; `src/include/zvec/db/options.h:60-62`) \u2192 `CollectionImpl::optimize` (`src/db/collection.cc:952`, passing `options.concurrency_` to `build_compact_task` at 988-990, which stores it in each `CompactTask`, `src/db/index/segment/segment_helper.h:54-66`) \u2192 `SegmentHelper::ExecuteCompactTask` \u2192 `ReduceVectorIndex(\u2026, task.concurrency_, \u2026)` (`segment_helper.cc:98, 148-150, 635`) \u2192 `MergeWithOptionalReuse(\u2026, concurrency, \u2026)` (`segment_helper.cc:668-670, 695-700, 743-745`).\n\n# 1. Pool selection per invocation\n\nThe selection is in `SegmentHelper::MergeWithOptionalReuse`, `src/db/index/segment/segment_helper.cc:799-812` (the identical logic for the create-index path is `src/db/index/segment/segment.cc:1549-1568`):\n\n- **A (`concurrency=0`)**: line 805-808 \u2014 `merge_options.pool = GlobalResource::Instance().optimize_thread_pool()` and `write_concurrency = pool->count()` (= 4). In core `Index::merge` (`src/core/interface/index.cc:1416-1446`), `options.pool != nullptr` \u2192 `reducer->set_thread_pool(options.pool)` (1437) and `effective_write_concurrency = min(4, 4)` (1438-1439). The merge runs on the **borrowed global optimize pool with 4 workers**.\n- **B (`concurrency=2`)**: `segment_helper.cc:809-811` sets only `write_concurrency = 2`; `pool` stays `nullptr`. `Index::merge` then creates a **per-call local pool**: `local_thread_pool = std::make_unique<ailego::ThreadPool>(2, false)` and `set_thread_pool(local_thread_pool.get())` (`index.cc:1434, 1440-1445`), with the declaration comment noting the local pool must outlive `reducer->reduce()`. It is destroyed when the merge returns.\n\n**B does not change the global pool**: nothing on the `concurrency > 0` path writes to `GlobalConfig` or `GlobalResource`; the global 4-worker pool (created once under `call_once`, `global_resource.cc:22-23`) is simply not referenced for B. `set_thread_pool` stores a raw pointer (`src/include/zvec/core/framework/index_reducer.h:172-175`), and the reducer hard-requires a pool (`src/core/mixed_reducer/mixed_streamer_reducer.cc:211-214`).\n\n# 2. Handoff to the builder and conversion training\n\nFor a builder-backed target, `MixedStreamerReducer::reduce` (`mixed_streamer_reducer.cc:206`) goes through `reduce_with_builder` (223; def 672) to `index_build` (739; def 742-780):\n\n- **Adapter**: `index_build` wraps the selected pool in `BorrowedSingleQueueIndexThreads(*thread_pool_)` (`mixed_streamer_reducer.cc:743-744`). That adapter holds a *reference* to the same `ailego::ThreadPool` (`src/include/zvec/core/framework/index_threads.h:174-225`); `count()` returns the underlying pool's count (184-186). So the builder-visible worker count is 4 under A, 2 under B \u2014 no new threads are created by the adapter.\n- **Optional conversion training immediately before**: `mixed_streamer_reducer.cc:745-747` calls `IndexConverter::TrainAndTransform(target_builder_converter_, target_holder, threads)`. The implementation (`src/core/framework/index_converter.cc:27-38`) passes the pool into `converter->train(two_pass_holder, std::move(threads))` (31), then `converter->transform(...)` (33).\n- **Builder train/build**: `mixed_streamer_reducer.cc:760` `target_builder_->train(threads, target_holder)` and `768` `target_builder_->build(std::move(threads), target_holder)`.\n\nThe pass-vs-consume distinction is explicit in the base classes: the default `IndexConverter::train(holder, threads)` does `(void)threads; return train(std::move(holder));` (`src/include/zvec/core/framework/index_converter.h:185-189`), and base `IndexRunner`'s `train`/`build` overloads leave `threads` an unnamed parameter (`src/include/zvec/core/framework/index_runner.h:692-695, 719-722`). So the reducer guarantees the pool is *offered*; consumption depends on the override. DiskAnnBuilder does consume it: `train(IndexThreads::Pointer, IndexHolder::Pointer)` at `src/core/algorithm/diskann/diskann_builder.cc:633` (fallback to a self-created pool only if `threads == nullptr`, 657-663 \u2014 not triggered here) and `build(...)` at 697 (same fallback 714-720), which passes `threads` to `build_internal` (def 304, submitting `threads->count()` tasks, 305-314), `prune_internal` (def 341-352), and `generate_quantized_data` (def 429; `thread_count = threads->count()` at 451-452; striped task group at 473-480).\n\n# 3. DiskANN PQ training: the outer chunk-dispatch pool is *not* reused\n\n`DiskAnnBuilder::train_quantized_data(IndexThreads::Pointer threads)` (`diskann_builder.cc:378-427`):\n\n- Lines 391-394, with the in-source comment *\"The quantizer creates its own pool, so bound it by the caller's pool\"*: `pq_thread_count = max(1, min(build_thread_count_, threads->count()))`, set as the quantizer's `\"thread_count\"` param (394) and consumed in `quantizer_->init` (396).\n- `build_thread_count_` is the builder's own setting: from `PARAM_DISKANN_BUILDER_THREAD_COUNT` (`diskann_builder.cc:51`), defaulting to `hardware_concurrency` when 0 (53-55).\n- `PqInt8Quantizer::init` reads it into `thread_count_` (`src/turbo/quantizer/pq_int8_quantizer/pq_int8_quantizer.cc:142`; member default 0, `pq_int8_quantizer.h:217`). `train` (232) reaches `train_all_chunks` (298/305; def 319), which at **322-323 constructs a fresh `SingleQueueIndexThreads(thread_count_, false)`** \u2014 a brand-new owned pool (`index_threads.h:113-116`: `size > 0` \u2192 exactly that many workers, subject to the `ThreadPool` clamp at `thread_pool.cc:93-101`) \u2014 and dispatches the `num_chunk_` sub-quantizer trainings round-robin across `pool_count = threads->count()` workers (328, 331-343).\n\nSo the PQ outer pool is a **separate, additional pool**, not the borrowed caller pool. Its worker count is `clamp(min(builder's build_thread_count_, caller pool count), \u22651, \u2264 hardware_concurrency)`: under A it is `min(build_thread_count_, 4)`, under B `min(build_thread_count_, 2)` \u2014 while the caller's pool workers sit idle waiting during PQ training.\n\n# 4. What the settings do and do not establish\n\n**Established (worker-pool capacity):**\n- `init(optimize_threads=4)` fixes the global optimize pool at 4 workers (validated > 0 at `python_config.cc:156` and `src/db/common/config.cc:83-86`; constructed at `global_resource.cc:27-29`).\n- Invocation A runs its merge on exactly those 4 global workers (`segment_helper.cc:805-808`; `index.cc:1436-1439`).\n- Invocation B runs its merge on a temporary 2-worker pool scoped to that `Index::merge` call (`index.cc:1440-1445`), and the global pool's configuration and worker count are unchanged by B.\n\n**Not established:**\n- **Whole-process thread count.** These knobs bound only the pools they configure. The process also holds the global query pool (`global_resource.cc:24-26`), the extra PQ-training pool created per DiskANN train (`pq_int8_quantizer.cc:322-323`), builder fallback pools if ever called with null threads (`diskann_builder.cc:657-663, 714-720`), plus Python/main/IO threads outside any of these pools. Nothing in this path caps the sum.\n- **Actual CPU utilization.** Worker counts are capacity, not usage: pool workers block on an empty queue when no tasks are submitted; the merge executes staged phases (convert-train \u2192 builder train \u2192 build/prune/PQ-encode) in which one pool can be idle while another runs; fan-out is bounded by work granularity (e.g., PQ chunk tasks loop `m = i; m < num_chunk_; m += pool_count` at `pq_int8_quantizer.cc:336-338`, so `num_chunk_ < pool_count` leaves workers idle); and consumption of the passed pool is only guaranteed where an override uses it (`index_converter.h:185-189`, `index_runner.h:692-695` show defaults that ignore it)."
  },
